  "why": "A photoelectric smoke alarm, its cover off, high on the living-room wall: a light beam crosses a dark chamber, smoke from a burning trash can drifts up, a side sensor catches the light the smoke bounces, a horn makes it loud, and a counter shows it lasts 10 years. The camera opens close on the dark chamber and its beam, frames the alarm with the smoke rising, and ends on the room.",
  "story": {
   "title": "How a smoke detector works",
   "hero": "a photoelectric smoke detector",
